  "Question": "If the perimeter of a rectangle is \\(p\\) and its diagonal is \\(d,\\) the difference between the length and width of the rectangle is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{8d^2-p^2}}2\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{8d^2+p^2}}2\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{6d^2-p^2}}2\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{6d^2+p^2}}2\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{8d^2-p^2}}4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Let the length and width be \\(L\\ge W>0\\). The perimeter gives their sum, while the diagonal forms a right triangle with the two sides. Thus\n\\[\nL+W=\\frac p2,\n\\qquad L^2+W^2=d^2.\n\\]\nWe want \\(L-W\\), so use a square identity that eliminates the unknown product \\(LW\\):\n\\[\n(L-W)^2=2(L^2+W^2)-(L+W)^2.\n\\]\nThis identity follows by expanding the squares. Substituting the known quantities gives\n\\[\n(L-W)^2=2d^2-\\frac{p^2}{4}\n=\\frac{8d^2-p^2}{4}.\n\\]\nSince \\(L-W\\ge0\\), take the nonnegative square root:\n\\[\n\\boxed{L-W=\\frac{\\sqrt{8d^2-p^2}}2}.\n\\]\nThe radicand is nonnegative because it equals \\(4(L-W)^2\\); it is zero when the rectangle is a square. The answer is choice A.",
